{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Let's start with the core job this site does for you. What's the ONE thing you most want it to do on day one — track spending across accounts, set and watch a budget, or plan/forecast (savings goals, debt payoff)? My recommendation: lead with expense tracking — logging transactions and seeing where your money goes — because it's the foundation every other finance feature builds on, and it gives us the cleanest thin slice to prove the skeleton and tests are wired together.","choices":["Track spending / transactions","Set and monitor a budget","Plan & forecast (goals, debt payoff)","Something else"],"recommended":"Track spending / transactions"},"prd":"# Mission: Foundation — Personal finance website\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up a running skeleton, a working test system, and one thin vertical slice proving both are connected — for a personal finance web app (scope TBD during Align).\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- (to be assembled during the interview)\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Building the actual finance product features (deferred to the project vision doc)\n\n**Constraints:**\n- (to be assembled during the interview)\n"}

